                  iMaze   version 1.3   Feburary 1996

              by  Hans-Ulrich Kiel  and  Joerg Czeranski
               at the Technical University of Clausthal


iMaze is a multi-player network action game for TCP/IP with 3D graphics
under X11/XView and Motif.  You run through a labyrinth and shoot other
players playing over the net and computer controlled ninjas.

The idea is taken from MidiMaze 2 on the Atari ST, although not all
features of MidiMaze 2 are implemented yet.

iMaze requires XView (OpenWindows) or Motif.  It was tested on
- - SunOS 4.1.3, OpenWindows       - SunOS 5.5, OpenWindows
- - SunOS 5.5, Motif               - Linux Slackware, OpenWindows
- - Ultrix 4.4, Motif              - HP-UX 9.05, Motif
- - DEC OSF/1 3.2C, Motif          - AIX 4.1.4, Motif
- - FreeBSD 2.1, OpenWindows       - SGI Irix v5.3, Motif
- - Sinix 5.41, Motif, GNU-make

New features of version 1.3:
- - Motif support
- - support for several new platforms
- - working sound for Linux and FreeBSD
- - most known bugs were fixed

The newest version is always available on ftp.tu-clausthal.de
(139.174.2.10) in the directory /pub/unix/games/imaze.

You can fetch it via
- - anonymous ftp,
- - fsp (port 21) or
- - email to mail-server@ftp.tu-clausthal.de.

We have also uploaded it to sunsite.unc.edu and ftp.x.org.

There is also a WWW page available at
http://www.tu-clausthal.de/student/iMaze/

The iMaze developers, Joerg Czeranski and Hans-Ulrich Kiel, can be
reached via email as:  imaze@tu-clausthal.de


