I have uploaded skim 0.8.4 to sunsite. You can find it in:

    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/skim-0.8.4.tgz

but it will soon move to:

    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/system/News/readers/skim-0.8.4.tgz

What's new in 0.8.4?
- --------------------
The main reason for releasing 0.8.4 was the upgrade to Tcl 7.4 and Tk 4.0. All 
current CD-ROM distributions of Linux use these new versions, and I got many 
requests to upgrade xskim. TclX is no longer required. I don't think xskim 
0.8.4 can still be used with older versions of Tcl/Tk.

Joel Young <jdyoung@erinet.com> provided most of the changes for Tcl 4.7 and
Tk 4.0. Some other users have send me diffs as well, but unfortunately I lost
these emails :-(

This is an overview of the most important changes. Details are in the README.

  - xskim now automatically saves the changes in the subject list when you 
    leave a newsgroup and it automatically saves the changes in an article 
    when you leave the article edit window.

  - In xskim you can now use the right mouse button to select/unselect the 
    selected subjects.

  - Skim no longer terminates whenever the news server returns an error.

  - The installation procedure now gives step-by-step instructions. Just type 
    'make' to get started.

  - Bug fixes and improvements in header line construction.

  - Changed from GNU to POSIX regular expression matching because of problems
    with the GNU functions. Unfortunately, this change may affect your 
    AutoSelect and Kill patterns.

LSM
