What:
The Linux Users' Group (LUG) at North Carolina State University (NCSU) will be
hosting a Linux Expo this Spring (Expo96).  We would like to invite you to come
to the Expo.  The theme we are centering on is "How has
Linux developed in the last year and where is it going?". 

When:
Saturday April 13, 1996

Where:
Centennial Campus of North Carolina State University in Raleigh, NC

Web Page--Registration and Information:
http://www.linux.ncsu.edu/

What will be there:
o Demos of Linux
o Speakers from the Linux community
o Products to purchase
o Other Linux enthusiasts

The LUG at NCSU held an Expo last year which attracted almost 300
attendees and well known people in the Linux community.  The success of 
last year's Expo far exceeded our expectations, and we are aiming at 
attracting an even bigger crowd this year.   As you well know, Linux has 
undergone dynamic changes in the last year.  The kernel has been ported 
to other platforms (most notably the Digital Alpha). In addition, the
kernel has greater functionality and the amount of high quality software
(both free and commercial) continues to grow.  We are hoping to attract, as
speakers to our Expo, the people who are making this happen.
  
- -------------------------------------------------------------

What:
Call for speakers for the Linux Expo 1996 brought to you by the Linux Users
Group at North Carolina State University.

Email address for interested speakers:
linux@ncsu.edu

The topics for the talks can either be technical or popular fitting into
the broad theme mentioned above.  If you are interested in participating
in the Linux Expo96 at NCSU, please reply  to linux@ncsu.edu, and indicate
what topic(s) you would be interested in giving a talk about.  Plan on
the talk being about 30-45 minutes in length, with some time for questions
after the presentation.

- -------------------------------------------------------------

What:
Call for vendors and sponsors for the Linux Expo 1996 brought to you by the 
Linux Users Group of North Carolina State University.

Email address for interested vendors and sponsors:
linux@ncsu.edu

What will be there:
o Demos of Linux
o Speakers from the Linux community
o Products to purchase
o Other Linux enthusiasts

For the LUG at NCSU
