-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


Dear Linux freaks,

a year ago we have written a LINUX driver for Advantech PCL-812PG. If
there is an interest we would like to place it in your information
domain to be accessible for more users. You

can find the driver at:

ftp://dec50.vm.stuba.sk/pub/csgrp/packages/advantech-PCL812PG-linux-driver/

or you can chcek co-author home page:

http://dec50.vm.stuba.sk:80/~hruz/soft.html

The PCL-812PG is not very fast card (30microsek for A/D conversion),
however we still thought that it is reasonable to work without
interrupt, which means that the driver waits in the first section
until the converion is finished. This concept was fully justified we
did not observe any problems or loss of system performance. The
locking of channels is fully implemented that means if one process
makes open() the channel is locked until the same process do not issue
close(). There is also a control of all card parameters via ioctl().
More info is in the driver doc.

In the case of further interest of some people over the net we ready to
assist in further improvements - adding full interrupt handlig or DMA
support.

				With Best Wishes
				Ludo Koren.


