[There are probably other systems like this around, but the
more there are, the lighter the load.]

Kernelmail: A simple kernel fetcher and deliverer

Tired of constantly ftpping to find the new kernel? Automate the process
instead. I've cobbled together a collection of scripts that work with
mirror, majordomo, and ncftp to allow you to get the latest kernel or
patch automatically. It saves tons of time and removes that day ruining
moment where you go looking for the new kernel and find there isn't a
new one yet.

New kernels and patches are either automatically downloaded by ncftp to 
your site, or delivered to you through the mail. The files are from a 
kernel mirror at <URL:ftp://linux.ucs.indiana.edu/pub/linux>.

Please look at 
<URL:http://linux.ucs.indiana.edu/linux/kernel/kernelmail.html>
for details on how it works and how to get yourself setup.

It's simple. It's free (of course it's free, it'd be downright immoral
for it not to be).

If you have questions or suggestions or problems contact me at 
cdent@indiana.edu

Enjoy,
Chris Dent


