The "ftp://ftp.craftwork.com/pub/v2.0/openwin.tar.gz" GNU zipped tar 
  file is available to work with ELF based (+ XFree-3.1.x) systems to
  provide a SUN OpenWindows(tm) runtime/development environment based
  on XView-3.2p1 and minimal open-look clients (olwm, cmdtool, ...)

    When unpacked it creates a "usr/openwin" directory hierarchy. By
  adding "/usr/openwin/lib" to /etc/ld.so.conf and subsequently updating
  symbolic links (i.e. issue, ldconfig) your ELF based Linux X window
  environment can have the same open-look-and-feel stock with SPARCstations.

  This is a binary distribution. The sources and Linux-ELF patches are
  readily available from sunsite.unc.edu and other Linux archives. This
  is being made available as a convinience to those not in a mood to
  build XView + clients. Linux archive administrators are encouraged
  to make this available, provided a notice is included (say, openwin.lsm)
  on its origin: Craftwork Solutions, Inc.

    Happy Trails



