I am happy to announce the release of e2fsprogs version 1.02.  It's
mostly a minor bugfix release with a new enhancements.  The main reason
for making this release is to because of a namespace conflict with the
include files with recent 1.3 kernels.  Version 1.02 has changes that
allow it to be compiled these latest 1.3 kernels.

The release notes and LSM entry for this package follow below.  Note
that I am still seeing bug reports from people who are still using
version 0.5b and 0.5c of this package.  Furthermore, there are some
distributions which are still using these older versiopns.  There are
severe bugs with these versions in how they handle certain types of
filesystem corruptions where e2fsck tries to relocate the inode or block
bitmaps, or the inode table.  People who are using older versions are
strongly encouraged to upgrade to the latest version of e2fsprogs.
Distribution maintainers are likewise strongly encouraged to include
this version of e2fsprogs in their release.

						- Ted


