-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


As some of you have noticed, the recently released version of e2fsprogs,
version 1.02, may fail a regression test --- f_dup2 --- when you compile
it from the source distribution.  This will happen if you compile it on
an ELF system; the problem is that e2fsck is calculating a floating
point number, and a.out and ELF systems are producing different results.
(6.2% versus 6.3%).  I generated the test case results using a a.out
binary, and so people compiling e2fsck using ELF will see a regression
test failure when the build process runs the e2fsck test suite.

You can ignore this test failure for 1.02; I'll fix this problem in the
next release, probably by not using floating point (which in general is
the correct solution to many problems :-).

For future reference, when reporting a problem with a failed test case,
look at the tests directory, and do a "ls *.failed".  For each test that
failed, the Makefile will generated a diff file comparing the expected
and actual output of e2fsck.  Please send me that diff file for any
failed tests; this will help me determine how and why the test case
failed.

Thanks!!

						- Ted


