Daniel O'Callaghan (danny@hilink.com.au) wrote:
: John Saunders wrote:
: > 
: > Just some quick info about how ISP groups handle accounting for on-line
: > time. I can see that with a fixed monthly price and x hours per day you
: > could simnply charge monthly and run a daemon to log people out after x
: > hours per day. With an hourly charged rate, are there SW packages out
: > there in PD land, or are they custom writtem programs?
: > 

I wrote one some time ago, it does most of what you want and then some,
although it is undergoing a major re-write now to interface directly
with my SQL backend. "Hidleho" does far more than just time tty's. It
also does cute various process/tty/security stuff too. It is 100% C and
mainly replaces the users login shell. It is FREE for NON-PROFIT,
NON-GOVERMENT use. The enhanced SQL version should be ready within a
month or so, however the current version should fit most people's needs
unless you are part of the Bezerkely Postgres project ;)

It currently does NOT calculate online charges, but it writes easily 
parseable accounting files for each user. As an example:

sh# ls -l /usr/hidleho/gun/
total 8
- -rw-------   1 root     sponsor         7 Dec 24 04:54 credit
- -rw-r--r--   1 hidleho  adm           105 Oct 12 07:36 environ
- -rw-r--r--   1 hidleho  unpaid         50 Feb 11 23:11 lastlogin
- -rw-r--r--   1 hidleho  unpaid         50 Feb 11 20:13 lastlogout
- -rw-r--r--   1 hidleho  unpaid          3 Feb 11 23:11 numlogins
- -rw-------   1 hidleho  adm           723 Oct 12 07:36 records
- -rw-r--r--   1 hidleho  unpaid         15 Feb 11 23:11 timeleft
- -rw-r--r--   1 hidleho  unpaid         17 Feb 11 20:13 totaltime
bash#
bash# cat /usr/hidleho/gun/numlogins
92
bash# cat /usr/hidleho/gun/totaltime
96029   1d2h40m29s
bash#

A user will see something like the following on login (if enabled):

Enter terminal type [vt100 rows 24 cols 80 erase ^H]:

*   HidleHo (v0.98) (c) 1993, 1994, 1995 Julian Assange  (Jan  1 1996) *

