CLUE Newsletter, February 1996
==============================

The Colorado Linux Users & Enthusiasts (CLUE), normally meets the
    third Thursday of every month. The next meeting will be at
    7:00pm on February 15th. The location will be Smoky Hill High
    School, located at 16100 E. Smoky Hill Rd. in southeast
    Aurora.

CLUE is for anyone with an interest in Linux, whether you are an
    expert, or just interested and want to know more about the
    Internet and Operating System phenomena that Linux
    represents. All interested parties are invited to attend.
    Let's learn from each other!

For more information, or to be added/removed from the CLUE
    mailing list contact Joel at 303-784-2795 or E-Mail:
    joel@mrg.uswest.com, or attend a meeting, and turn in your
    information there. There is no cost for membership or
    newsletter subscription via E-Mail. 
    
Future Meeting dates will be: 
    Q1/96  March 21
    Q2/96  April 18, May 16, June 20...

Directions to Smoky Hill High School:  Take Parker south from
    I-225, to Quincy.  There will be a shopping center on the
    left, and a Stoplight. Take a left on Quincy. Then the first
    stoplight with a right turn will be Smoky Hill Road.  Turn
    right onto Smoky Hill, cross Chambers (a light), and then
    turn right at Laredo (a stop light), then left into the
    School parking lot. Go past the main entrance, and to the
    activities entrance.

Vendors are encouraged to attend, make Linux-related
    announcements, etc. 
    
Questions and Information: joel@mrg.uswest.com


Topics:
    February News
    CLUE Linux CD Library
    Presenters Needed
    Help Wanted/For Hire/Wanted/For Sale
    Administrivia/Credits


February News
- -------------
    
    At the February meeting we will have representatives from
    Stonehenge Internet. A local (Denver) Internet provider which
    uses Linux for its primary servers. They will talk about the
    services they offer, and their experiences with Linux as an
    internet server.

    In March we are expecting representatives from XInside - makers
    of the Accelerated X product - to join us to talk about 
    their product, history with Linux, and outlook for the future.

    If you have any announcements or news for this section of the
    newsletter, please send it to the editor, joel@mrg.uswest.com


CLUE Linux CD Library
- ---------------------

    CLUE maintains a "library" of donated CD distributions.  CLUE
    meeting attendees are free to take any distributions they would
    like to try from the library, and are encouraged to donate
    unneeded distributions.  The library's goal is to encourage
    experimentation with Linux for those who have not yet tried it,
    and to enable easy trial of unfamiliar distributions.
    
    Don Lewis is currently the CLUE Librarian.


Presenters Needed
- -----------------

    We would like your ideas for presenters/speakers, and topics for
    both Meeting presentations, and also Newsletter articles.  Please
    help; supply either or both for us.  Volunteers are especially
    appreciated.


Help Wanted/For Hire/Wanted/For Sale
- ------------------------------------

