This is to announce a network driver for the SMC 9xxx chipset. This is 
used by a seemingly small variety of VLBUS and PCI cards.  

The driver should work nicely on a SMC9192 or a SMC9194, and maybe 
it will work on the 100baseT SMC91C100. 

To obtain this driver:

 ftp://fenris.campus.vt.edu/smc9/smc9.tar.gz
 ftp://sfbox.vt.edu/filebox/F/fenris/smc9/smc9.tar.gz


This driver has the following known misfeatures:

  (1)  IRQ is undetected :  This should work, but sometimes it won't find the
  IRQ.  Either specify it on the command line with irq=xx or run it a couple
  of times.

  (2)  Multicast support gives a warning and isn't using hardware filtering.
  The warning should be removed, as this is what most of the other drivers do,
  hardware filtering is possible, but I can't test it at the present time.

  (3) The hardware IP address isn't setable.   This is just a minor detail
  that will be added someday. 
 

 For more information on this, I can be contacted at : 
	
   erik@fenris.campus.vt.edu (running on this driver half the time ;)  )
   erik@mail.vt.edu 

   


