Hy folks,

	we are happy to announce that we now have VLB (Verzeichniss
	lieferbarer Buecher) also known as G-BIP (German Books in
	Print) running under Linux.

	At autum book fair in Frankfurt I went to the major vendors
	of CD-ROM bibliographies and asked them for a linux port
	of their dos based CD-ROM database programs.

	My main argument was that a Linux port will help all unix
	based book shops, as its very cheap the have a linux box
	aside.

	So we are now happy that VLB is running, VLZ (Verzeichniss
	lieferbarer Zeitschriften) Bowker alias BIP (Books in Print)
	will come rsn.

	We hope that this will be a break thru argument for the
	other vendors of CD-ROM bibliographies.

	Many thanks to Peter Moser of Buchhandes Verein Germany
	Bernd Stehle of /usr Software Entwicklung GmbH, and Gleen
	Kessler of Reed Reference Publishing.

By Michael

