     **************************
     *  ICAO Map version 1.0  *
     **************************

What is ICAO Map?
- -----------------
ICAO Map is an interactive program running under X11/Motif. Its
input is a so called "world file", which is an ASCII file
containing descriptions of objects such as airports, roads,
towns, radio beacons and the like. ICAO Map will use either
Lambert or Mercator projection to generate a map from this
world file, either on your screen or as PostScript output.

ICAO Map allows you to interactively work with the map on the
screen, i.e. scroll it, use a rubber line to measure distances
and tracks etc. Additional features are available for both
motorized flights and soaring.

Version 1.0 is the most recent version
that has been released. Though ICAO Map is copyrighted software,
it may be copied and used free of charge. See the
licencing information in the ICAO Map manual.

ICAO Map has been reported to compile (with minor
changes in some cases) on Linux,
Ultrix, SunOS, Solaris, HP-UX and on SGI systems.


What is new in version 1.0?
- ---------------------------
 * display of logged flights
 * evaluation of climbing
 * barogram display
 * 3 dimensional airspace structure 
 * selectable units for altitudes and distances
 * user configuration file
 * multiple world files can be loaded
 * GPS simulator (produces NMEA protocol output)
 * lot's of tiny details improve

See also: http://www.oih.rwth-aachen.de/icao.html


Where can I find it?
- --------------------
ftp: ventus.oih.rwth-aachen.de,
     /icao/icao-1.0

What you'll find is:

icao-README      this file
icao-data.tgz    German data base and sample flight logs
icao-doc.tgz     Postscript manual
icao-src.tgz     full source code and Makefile

For Linux, there are also binaries available.
You will only need ONE of the following files:

linux-binaries/
  icao-a.out-static.gz    old a.out format, with Motif
  icao-a.out.gz           old a.out format, requires Motif
  icao-elf-static.gz      new ELF format, with Motif
  icao-elf.gz             new ELF format, requires Motif


Enjoy the program!

